       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,600 mg/day of ibuprofen is a toxic dose, and I don't know of any indication that calls for it. There's no dosing regimen where it would be safe for a 70 kg adult, even with normal kidney and liver function. Entering it could lead to serious harm before anyone catches it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day). The maximum is 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Enter a dose above the usual limit if you have a specific rationale.** Give me the dose and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. I would still suggest pharmacy review first.\n- **Help with something else.** If pain or inflammation control is the goal, I can help you enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n\nIf I've misunderstood and you meant a different dose, tell me the correct one and I'll enter it right away."
